course: dictionary
lesson: 2483
title: Short forms and abbreviations
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short way of writing a longer word or phrase. DC is short for more than one thing, so the words around it show you which meaning to use. In «Some capitals were planned from scratch to be fair between regions: Washington DC in the 1790s», the sentence is about cities and capitals, so DC means District of Columbia.
explain: The topic is your first clue. A sentence about batteries and electricity means DC is direct current. A sentence about superheroes means DC is DC Comics. A sentence about police means DC is Detective Constable. Always ask: what is this text about?
explain: Then test your meaning. Swap the longer phrase into the sentence instead of the short form. If «Washington District of Columbia in the 1790s» still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Check the capital letters too: dc, d.c. and DC are all written forms of the same short form.
fact: An abbreviation is a shortened form of a word or phrase.
fact: «DC» can mean direct current, electricity that flows in one direction, as from a battery.
fact: «D.C.» means District of Columbia, the capital city of the United States, as in Washington, D.C.
fact: «DC» can also mean DC Comics, the American company known for Superman and Batman.
fact: In music, «D.C.» means «da capo», Italian for go back to the beginning.
exercise: «Some capitals were planned from scratch to be fair between regions: Washington DC in the 1790s.» What does DC stand for here? | Direct current | Detective Constable | DC Comics | *District of Columbia
exercise: In a science lesson, the teacher says a battery gives DC, which flows in one direction. What does DC stand for? | District of Columbia | Dinner Club | Detective Constable | *Direct current
exercise: Find and copy one abbreviation from this list. | capitals | regions | *DC | planned
test: Ella reads about Superman in a DC comic. What does DC mean here? | District of Columbia | Direct current | *DC Comics, an American comic company | Detective Constable
test: In sheet music, you see «D.C.» at the end of a line. What does it tell you to do? | *Go back to the beginning | Play faster | Turn the page to the end | Stop playing for ever
exam: Ben's police book says, «The DC arrived at the scene.» What does DC mean here? | District of Columbia | Direct current | DC Comics | *Detective Constable
